-- title:
--   Regularity at all new places forces membership in K'· F
-- statement:
--   Let $K, F, K', F'$ be fields with $F$ an algebra over $K$, $F'$ an algebra over $K'$, together with algebra maps $K \to K'$, $F \to F'$ and $K \to F'$ making both $K \to K' \to F'$ and $K \to F \to F'$ scalar towers, and assume $K$ and $K'$ are algebraically closed. Assume $F$ is a one-variable function field over $K$ in the sense that some $x \in F$ is transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over $K(x)$, and likewise for $F'$ over $K'$. Assume further that $F$ is a curve over $K$ and $F'$ a curve over $K'$, i.e. in each case: every nonzero function $f$ has a divisor $D$ with $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ at every place $v$ and $\deg D = 0$; every place has residue field finite over the base field; and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one over the function field. Here a place of $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring. Assume the image of $F$ generates $F'$ over $K'$, i.e. the intermediate field of $F'/K'$ generated by the range of $F \to F'$ is all of $F'$. Let $z \in F'$ be such that $z$ lies in the valuation ring of every place $v'$ of $F'/K'$ whose valuation ring contracts along $F \to F'$ to the valuation ring of no place of $F/K$. Then $z$ lies in the $K'$-span of the image of $F$ in $F'$.
--
--   This is the classical statement that a function on a constant field extension $F' = K'\cdot F$ which is regular at every place of $F'/K'$ not lying over a place of $F/K$ already belongs to $K' \cdot F$ (Chevalley; Stichtenoth, Theorem 3.6.3), here in a form free of any hypothesis on the characteristic, both base fields being algebraically closed. It is the substantive input to the results identifying $L_{K'}(\mathrm{Con}\,D)$ with the $K'$-span of the image of $L_K(D)$ and comparing the corresponding dimensions under constant field extension.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_mem_span_range_algebraMap_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed.lean

import Mathlib
